-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",193,{
[6145]="7003A95C\n1\tDeliver the torn skins to a collection box\030Collect torn skins (total: 10)\tYou have accepted a task to acquire trophies from battle.\n",
[6146]="700011CA\n1\tFind Muiladan\tMuiladan waits in the valley to the south. Areneth asked you to escort Muiladan, a scout from Esteldín, to the Ranger-encampment at Gath Forthnír.\n2\tTalk to Areneth\tAreneth is at Gath Forthnír to the north. Muiladan survived the journey north and will be able to lead his companions to the hidden camp.\n",
[6147]="7006565B\n1\tThere are thirsty labourers working in Halach. Gorhir has asked you to bring water-skins to them.\t\n2\tTalk to Gorhir\tYou have finished delivering water-skins to thirsty labourers in Halach. You should talk to Gorhir at the pier.\n",
[6148]="70060E11\n1\tComfort the needy pig with a pat\030Feed the hungry chicken\030Feed the hungry cat\030Comfort the needy hound with a pat\030Comfort the needy cow with a pat\030Feed the hungry goat\030Feed the hungry pony\tNeedy and hungry animals can be found in the village of Long Cleeve. You should care for the needy and hungry animals in Long Cleeve.\n2\tTalk to Prunella Goldworthy\tPrunella Goldworthy can be found in the village of Long Cleeve. You should talk to Prunella Goldworthy.\n3\tTend to the injured bird\030Tend to the injured frog\030Tend to the injured rabbit\030Tend to the injured tortoise\tInjured animals can be found in the village of Long Cleeve. You should care for the injured animals in Long Cleeve.\n4\tTalk to Prunella Goldworthy\tPrunella Goldworthy can be found in the village of Long Cleeve. You should talk to Prunella Goldworthy.\n",
[6149]="70027182\n1\tCollect red clover at Hen Turrau (total: 10)\tRed clover can be found in the hills near the mine, particularly at Hen Turrau. Melvun has asked you to collect red clover which he can use to make medicines for the injured miners.\n2\tBring the red clover to Melvun at the mine\tMelvun is at the Barnavon Mine. You should bring the red clover you collected to Melvun.\n3\tTalk to Melvun at the mine\tMelvun is at the Barnavon Mine. You should speak with Melvun again to see if he has finished the salve.\n4\tThe wounded miners can be found in the camp outside the Barnavon Mine. Melvun asked you to take the salve and bandages to the wounded miners and bind their wounds.\t\n5\tTalk to Melvun at the mine\tMelvun is at the Barnavon Mine. You should speak with Melvun and let him know that you have completed his task.'\n",
[6150]="7004CE40\n1\tCure poisoned birds (total: 2)\030Cure poisoned frogs (total: 2)\030Cure poisoned rabbits (total: 3)\030Cure poisoned squirrels (total: 3)\030Cure poisoned foxes (total: 2)\tPoisoned animals can be found north of the path in Eryn Lasgalen. You should cure poisoned animals.\n2\tComplete\tCompleted.\n",
[6151]="7006B5FA\n1\tCollect rice stalks (total: 8)\tYou have been asked to collect stalks of rice that are ready to harvest from the eastern fields at Ekagar.\n2\tBring rice stalks to Urama\tYou have collected stalks of rice that were ready to harvest from the fields to the east. You should bring them to Urama by the trellis.\n",
[6152]="70059773\n1\tHunt wild game at Helva's Edge\tBeasts can be found at Helva's Edge in the Wildwood. You should hunt wild game at Helva's Edge.\n2\tHunt wild game at Helva's Edge (total: 6)\tBeasts can be found at Helva's Edge in the Wildwood. You should hunt wild game at Helva's Edge.\n",
[6153]="70043E04\n1\tSteal escaped chickens (total: 10)\tEscaped Chickens can be found roaming around Western Osgiliath. You should steal the escaped chickens.\n2\tBring the chickens to Dulglok\tDulglok is at Shrak Mauruk. You should bring the chickens to Dulglok.\n",
[6154]="7001B1D0\n1\tTalk to Éogar at the Hengstacer Farm\tHengstacer Farm lay north-east of Saeradan's Cabin, up the eastward road from the Old Greenway Fort. Saeradan sent you to the Hengstacer Farm to investigate talk of Orcs.\n2\tTalk to Cam Applewood at the Hengstacer Farm\tCam Applewood is at the Hengstacer Farm. Éogar told you to speak with Cam Applewood, his farmhand.\n",
[6155]="70022709\n1\tTalk to Éogar at Hengstacer Farms\tYou should make your way to Hengstacer farms and speak with the owner Éogar. From the West-gate of Bree travel north along the Greenway until you pass Thornley's Farm on your left and an old ruined fort on your right. There is a thin trail, beaten by the hooves of Hengstacer horses and ponies that leads up the hill beside those ruins. Follow that trail to the east and north, and you will find your way to Hengstacer Farms.\n",
[6156]="70043DAC\n1\tCollect Escaped Chickens (total: 10)\tEscaped Chickens can be found roaming around Western Osgiliath. You should find the escaped chickens.\n2\tBring the Chickens to the Chicken coop\tThe Chicken coop is located outside the Palace of Eldacar. You should bring the Chickens to the Chicken coop.\n3\tSpeak to Cangoras\tCangoras is at the Palace of Eldacar. You should speak to Cangoras.\n",
[6157]="7004A8E9\n1\tBurn webs in Cirith Ungol (total: 10)\tWebs can be found throughout Cirith Ungol. Legolas has asked you to burn webs to prevent the spiders from gaining a foothold in Cirith Ungol.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have burned many webs in Cirith Ungol.\n",
[6158]="70016B8D\n1\tDefeat Nûst\tNûst is at Drû-garmadh to the south-east. Alrekur believes if Nûst, Drû-garmadh's leader, is defeated, the camp will no longer provide a threat.\n2\tTalk to Alrekur at Mekhem-bizru\tAlrekur is at Mekhem-bizru, north-west of Drû-garmadh. Alrekur will be pleased to hear Nûst has been defeated.\n",
[6159]="70026FCA\n1\tDefend the herald of the Rohirrim\tThe herald is supposed to be travelling towards Dol Baran from an encampment at the Ford of Isen. You should find and defend the herald of the Rohirrim.\n2\tCheck on the Rohirrim herald\tThe body of the fallen Rohirrim herald lies before you. You should collect the fallen herald's horn and return it to Grimbold.\n3\tTalk to Grimbold at the Ford of Isen\tThe Ford of Isen demarks the eastern boundary of Dunland. The Rohirrim have established an encampment on the western side of the ford, where Grimbold of the Grimslade can be found commanding their local forces. Bring the horn to Grimbold and tell him of the herald's fate.\n",
[6160]="7005403D\n1\tRaise heraldry of Durin IV in Parth Daenath (total: 6)\tGood places to raise the heraldry of Durin IV can be found in Parth Daenath. You should raise the heraldry of Durin IV in Parth Daenath.\n2\tTalk to Durin IV\tDurin IV can be found at Echad-in-Edhil. You should talk to Durin IV.\n",
[6161]="7005403B\n1\tRaise heraldry of Gil-galad in Parth Daenath (total: 2)\030Raise heraldry of Eryn Galen in Parth Daenath (total: 2)\030Raise heraldry of Lothlórien in Parth Daenath (total: 2)\tYou should raise heraldry of Gil-galad, Eryn Galen, and Lothlórien in Parth Daenath to intimidate the Enemy and boost the spirits of the soldiers.\n2\tTalk to Celeborn\tCeleborn can be found in Echad-in-Edhil. You should talk to Celeborn.\n",
[6162]="70053F50\n1\tRaise heraldry of the High King in Arandor (total: 6)\tYou should place heraldry of the High King in Arandor to intimidate the Enemy and boost the spirits of the soldiers.\n2\tTalk to Eärtur\tEärtur can be found at Adambel. You should talk to Eärtur.\n",
[6163]="70058BB8\n1\tDestroy banners of Gorgar at Bagûd-mekhem (total: 10)\tBanners of Gorgar can be found at Bagûd-mekhem. You have discovered bloody banners flown by the Orcs loyal to Gorgar the Ruthless at Bagûd-mekhem. You should destroy them.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have destroyed many banners of Gorgar at Bagûd-mekhem.\n",
[6164]="70053F4D\n1\tRaise heraldry of the Thíuda in Arandor (total: 5)\tGood places to raise the heraldry of the Thíuda can be found in Arandor. You should raise the heraldry of the Thíuda for Huneric.\n2\tTalk to Huneric\tHuneric can be found in Adambel. You should talk to Huneric.\n",
[6165]="70014812\n1\tTalk to Sigdan at the Chamber of the Cross-roads\tSigdan is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, north of the Dolven-view. Rambi told you to speak to his friend Sigdan about the armour you found.\n2\tTalk to Rambi in the Chamber of the Cross-roads\tRambi is at the Chamber of the Cross-roads in Durin's Way. Sigdan has given his evaluation of the scratches in the armour you found.\n",
[6166]="7004D70A\n1\tTroubled Dale-folk can be found throughout Dale. Erna has asked you to speak to a number of troubled Dale-folk and learn if there is any truth to the rumours that have been spreading in Dale.\t\n2\tFind the rumour-monger in Dale\tThe rumour-monger can be found somewhere in Dale. You have listened to the tales of several troubled Dale-folk, and it seems that a Lake-man has come to Dale telling wild stories of the Herald of Winter. You should seek the rumour-monger in Dale.\n3\tTalk to the rumour-mongering Lake-man\tThe rumour-mongering Lake-man can be found in Dale. You have found the rumour-monger telling wild tales to a crowd of nearby Dale-folk. You should speak to him and urge him to stop spreading dangerous rumours.\n4\tTalk to Kynlig in Dale\tKynlig can be found fishing in Dale. The rumour-monger claims the story was told to him by a dwarf named Kynlig in Dale. You should find and speak to Kynlig.\n5\tTalk to Erna\tErna can be found in Dale. You learned that the Lake-man misunderstood Kynlig's tale and that the Herald of Winter is little more than a legend to the Dwarves of Erebor. You should return to Erna and tell her what you have learned.\n6\tFind the Lake-man along the road to Lake-town and deliver him to the Queen Regent\tThe Lake-man can likely be found along the roadway to Lake-town. Erna has asked that you seek the Lake-man on the roadway to Lake-town and deliver him to her in Dale.\n7\tTalk to Erna and warn her of Karazgar's interest in the Herald of Winter\tErna can be found in Dale. The Lake-man was slain along the roadway by one of Karazgar's agents in the Dale-lands. It seems Karazgar has a peculiar interest in the Herald of Winter. You should return to Erna and tell her what has occurred.\n8\tDeliver Erna's missive to King Thorin III in Erebor\tKing Thorin III can be found in Erebor. Erna has written a missive to King Thorin III and has asked you to deliver it to him in the halls of Erebor.\n",
[6167]="70001847\n1\tCollect meadowsweet (total: 5)\030Collect periwinkle (total: 5)\030Collect butterbur (total: 5)\tPeriwinkle can be found among rock outcroppings atop the hills of Nan Amlug, near Othrikar. Meadowsweet can be found in south facing tree roots in the spider-camp south of Esteldín. Butterbur can be found growing along the waters edge in the fens near the Elf-refuge of Lin Giliath in Meluinen. You should gather herbs for Orthonn.\n2\tBring the herbs to Orthonn\tOrthonn is in Kingsfell, north of Gatson's Farm. You should bring the herbs you gathered to Orthonn.\n",
[6168]="70059787\n1\tCollect wild herbs (total: 10)\tWild herbs can be found in the southern edge of the Wildwood. You should collect wild herbs.\n2\tPlace the wild herbs in a storage crate\tA storage crate can be found in either Trader's Wharf or Trestlebridge. You should place the wild herbs in a storage crate.\n",
[6169]="70003811\n1\tDefeat lynx in the Vale of Thrain (total: 10)\tLynx can be found throughout the Vale of Thráin, but Óláfr suggested heading north to the Thrushstones. Óláfr has asked you to secure the safety of the road leading through the Vale of Thráin by hunting the lynx that dwell there.\n2\tTalk to Óláfr at Noglond\tÓláfr is at Noglond in Thrain's Vale, south along the road from the Thrushstones. Óláfr should be pleased to hear of your success.\n",
[6170]="7002D72E\n1\tCheck on the horse from Combe\tThe horse from Combe is on the far side of Hengstacer Farm's main stable area from Éogar.\n",
[6171]="7002D72F\n1\tCheck on the horse from Combe\tThe horse from Combe is on the far side of Hengstacer Farm's main stable area.\n",
[6172]="7002D730\n1\tCheck on the Horse from Combe\tThe Horse from Combe is on the far side of the horse farm's main stable area from Éogar.\n",
[6173]="7004541E\n1\tSpeak with Herefara\tHerefara can be found in the War-stead of the Helmingas. You should speak with Herefara.\n2\tPatrol the river crossing to the Beacon Hills\030Patrol Nardol's look-out\030Patrol Nardol\030Patrol Eilenach's beacon\030Patrol Eilenach\030Use the whistle to summon your new friend if you become separated\tYou should patrol Taur Drúadan with Herefara by your side.\n3\tTalk to Herefara to dismiss him\030Use the whistle to summon your new friend if you become separated\tSpeak with Herefara.\n4\tSpeak with Herefara\tHerefara can be found in the War-stead of the Helmingas. You should speak with Herefara.\n",
[6174]="700018A0\n1\tCollect the skull of the Great Aurochs\tThe skull of The Great Aurochs is being held in the lands of the Rauta-lehmä, eastward across Nan Amlug. In order to prove his benign intent to the Earth-kin, Ragnarr Hornsounder has asked you to retrieve the stolen skull of The Great Aurochs from the Rauta-lehmä.\n2\tTalk to Ragnarr Hornsounder\tRagnarr Hornsounder is at the camp of the Suuri-lehmä, west of the Rauta-lehmä camp. You should return the skull of the Great Aurochs to Ragnarr Hornsounder.\n",
[6175]="70001849\n1\tTalk to Gilmar at Gatson's Farm\tAn heir to Bardulf Gilmar may yet be found somewhere in the North Downs.\n2\tTalk to Orthonn at Ost Lagoros\tOrthonn is at the ruins of Ost Lagoros, north-west of Gatson's Farm. You found a stone marker bequeathing land to the forebear of Gatson's workhand, Gilmar. Gilmar has asked you to ask the Ranger Orthonn about his forebear.\n3\tTalk to Istuienn at Esteldín\tIstuienn is at Esteldín, east of Gatson's farm. You found a stone marker bequeathing land to the forebear of Gatson's workhand, Gilmar. Gilmar sent you to speak to the Ranger Orthonn, but Orthonn was unable to help. He did, however, suggest you seek Istuienn, the archivist at Esteldín.\n4\tBring the excerpt to Gilmar at Gatson's Farm\tGilmar is at Gatson's farm. Istuienn, who keeps the Rangers' archives, provided you an excerpt of some old chronicles explaining how Gilmar's ancestor saved the life of Eärnur, an ancient Prince of Gondor, and was granted land in perpetuity for his valour.\n",
[6176]="7006E176\n1\tTalk to Lubathred\tElf notaries can be found in Duillond or Rivendell.\n",
})
